# No patches on real connection

The owner requires **durable, proper fixes** for anything that touches **real infrastructure, production, or live API/network behavior**.

This rule works with `no-patches-proper-implementation-only.mdc`. Together they mean: **never patch; fix the owner.**

## Forbidden (especially when not localhost / mock)

- Stopgap patches that paper over contract mismatches instead of fixing server + client alignment
- Client-only shims that mask missing or wrong server responses on real hosts
- Silent catch-and-ignore on real auth, wallet, payments, DB, or streaming paths
- Fake success, placeholder data, or stubbed responses against the real backend
- Time-bomb TODO hacks presented as finished behavior for production
- Consuming IAP / crediting coins / joining LiveKit / mutating wallet without an honest verified success path

## Required

- **One clear contract** between client and server (types, explicit normalization, documented JSON shapes)
- **Server** owns authoritative balances, purchases, and permissions; **client** validates/normalizes explicitly
- Fail visibly (correct errors) rather than hide failures on real connections
- Prefer the smallest change that is still **honest and complete**, not the smallest hack
- Fix lifecycle at the owner (`auth` store, `roomSocket`, `LiveKitSession`, payment verify modules) — do not scatter workarounds in screens

## Local / dev only

- Short-lived debugging or mocks are acceptable **only** when clearly scoped to local/dev and cannot affect production/store builds or real URLs unless explicitly requested

Default: **never patch the app in a way that lies to real users or real backends.**
